{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/812482-2e-ashoka-bloodline","id":812482,"title":"[2e] Ashoka bloodline","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-20T03:51:06-08:00","id":812482,"title":"[2e] Ashoka bloodline","content":"Hello everyone. it is my first try at the Bloodline for the 2ed and the second ever. So I'll need some help concerning Devotions and even bloodline gift/banes (I've a somewhat clear idea, but I'm not sure to know if the Gift is truly one in the 2e rules). it is pretty much work in progress, which will be completed with everyone help ! <div align=\"center\"><u><b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Ashoka</span></b></u></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Background :</b> As a bloodline, the Ashoka were recognized in 1848 by the Kindred of London, when three generations demonstrated the same peculiar bane and favour for the Auspex Discipline. The history of the Ashoka trace back to the Embrace of Robert Wallace Johnson in 1760. R.W. Johnson was a member of the East India Company and among its first members to be dispatched to India proper. There, he quickly attracted the attention of a former Londoner Ventrue neonate, who was intending to forge his own Domain far from his homeland. For almost fifty years, Wallace spent his unlive in India, feeling profoundly dead, spiritually. It was only when he moved to Ceylon to flee conflicts with native Vampires in India that he began to reclaim some sense of spiritual belonging. Once one the island, he was shaken by the Theravadin Buddhism which still exists on this country. He delved into this religion history and myths, and discovered the existence of King Ashoka, depicted as the perfect Buddhist King. Like the ancient King of Northern India, Robert W. Johnson wanted to embrace Buddhism without becoming a monk. Feeling that he needed more merits that he could have obtained by himself to become a great ruler, he Embraced a local devout and spent ten years studying what he could of Theravada.<br /> <br /> Johnson returned to England in 1820, with three Childe, two of English origin, where he spent twenty-eight years integrating himself both in the Vampiric society of London, and in the esoteric groups of mortals. He specifically created ties to the various Orientalist groups and he and his brood seemed almost desperate to create strong connections. It was only in 1848 that it was discovered that Robert and his Childe had become a specific bloodline, when his first grand-childe was Embraced and displayed the same characteristic inability to create any blood bond of any kind, whether to mortals or Kindred. Since then, the Ashoka have joined the Ordo Dracul, apparently hoping to transcend the vampiric condition to truly become proper buddhist rulers of the Night, as their eponym was two centuries before Christ. The usage of Auspex seems to come with great ease to the Wise Rulers, because they are seeking personal illumination, if the Ashoka are to be believed.<br /> <br /> Since the Ashoka pursue a quest to Nirvana, they thrive to free themselves from the Beast completely. Therefore, as Vampires, they have devised a way to better themselves, trying to become Arhant of the Night, which is a necessary step for them to reach Nirvana. Having to deal with the Vampiric condition, and strongly believing that only humans can achieve freedom from the Samsara, they work hard to expunge themselves from the Beast. Such goal as lead to an almost aloof condition among the Ashoka, one which set them apart for the Kindred<br /> <br /> <b>The Becoming :</b> The Ashoka are drawn to those they believe would be fitting rulers for the Kindred but who need the gentle hand of the Three Jewels to truly surpass their potential. As of today, they still mostly Embrace people who were merchants, bankers, traders, as their founder was a member of the East India Company. Usually, the Ashoka also seek out those who are seeking something more in their life, without being able to quite tell what they search. Charisma and ambitions are sorely needed in the bloodline, both to compensate their Bane, and to promote their position in the Danse Macabre and the Ordo Dracul. As of today, most of the Merchants are still in the British Isles, but some can be found in France, Germany, North America and Australia.<br /> <br /> <b>In the Danse Macabre :</b> The Ashoka form the largest bloodline of Western Vampires proclaiming ties to Buddhism instead of Abrahamic faiths. Therefore, they are, at best, shunned by the members of the Lancea Sanctum, or actively hunted down as heretics. The position of the Invictus and the Carthians is somewhat more ambiguous : on the one hand, the religious foundations of the bloodline indispose both those Covenants, but each of them recognize that the Merchants posses a great deal of knowledges and influences which would be better used serving the Covenants than in the hands of any other faction. The Circle doesn't seems to hold interest into the Ashoka, but rumours abound about Acolytes hunting down or luring Wise Rulers to feed them to their strange Elders deep in the wild. However, it is the Ordo Dracul which boast by far the greater number of Merchants, since they posses ties to the Eastern world which makes them invaluable in the discovery of new ways to transcend the Vampiric Condition, even if their tendency to bring back everything to the goal of becoming Arhat tends to create unnecessary tensions. Being somewhat ancient, some Ashoka are also among the Unaligned, where they try their best to hide their condition, fearing to attract blood addicts and diablerists.<br /> <br /> <b>Parent Clan :</b> Ventrue<br /> <b>Disciplines :</b> Dominate, Animalism, Resilience, Auspex<br /> <b>Nicknames : </b>Wise Rulers, Merchants (derogatory)<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline gift :</b> <b>The Detachment from the Beast</b><br /> The Ashoka do not feel the pull of their Beast as strongly as other Vampires. They have a +2 bonus to resist any kind of Frenzy.<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Curse : The Bondless</b><br /> The Merchants are unable to create ghouls, blood puppets or Vinculum. Furthermore, while their blood still makes addicts out of other Vampires, the Amaranth of an Ashoka doesn't leave a mark on the soul of the diablerist. Those reasons explains both the discretion of the Wise Rulers when they feel not safe enough and their drive to transcend their condition.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","user":"Ur-Than","date":". 02-05-2016, 12:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T09:40:32-08:00","id":812681,"title":"","content":"Hello. Are you looking for feedback on this? Please take no offense if you arent. RAW says new devotions cost the dots of the requirements cut in half. that devotion would cost 4 exp. 8 is a lot as its very very close to what dominate can do already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T09:41:56-08:00","id":812683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/812482-2e-ashoka-bloodline#post812482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello everyone. it is my first try at the Bloodline for the 2ed and the second ever. So I'll need some help concerning Devotions and even bloodline gift/banes (I've a somewhat clear idea, but I'm not sure to know if the Gift is truly one in the 2e rules). it is pretty much work in progress, which will be completed with everyone help ! <div align=\"center\"><u><b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Ashoka</span></b></u></div><br /> <b>Bloodline gift :</b> <b>The Detachment</b><br /> Since the Ashoka pursue a quest to Nirvana, they posses only two Touchstones, instead of three; furthermore, when they have to make a test of Derangement because of the death or destruction of a Touchstones, the 1 doesn't subtract a success.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, one thing, <b>1 doesn't subtract successes, not even in first edition</b>. That is Vampire: The Masquerade that had that.<br /> <br /> Second, what do you mean only 2 touchstones? Vampires start with <b>one</b> touchstone and can purchase more as a merit up to <b>five</b> more, and touchstones are GOOD things. As a gift you don't want to steal merits from players. Dertangements aren't a thing in 2nd Edition, they were replaced with persistent conditions, (Languid being the one that you get from losing a touchstone, it makes you sleepy). If you meant Degeneration, the loss is a choice in this situation, no roll.<br /> <br /> Basically your gift is an additional penalty at best since the only current rule it involves is the number of touchstones, which are GOOD things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T10:08:23-08:00","id":812696,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the feedbacks, both of you. I haven't B&amp;S yet, so I did my best with what I could get my hands on. The idea of the &quot;Gift&quot; is basically that the Ashoka wants to give up earthy attachment while &quot;ruling&quot; but I've no idea how to translate it as a gift...<br /> <br /> As for the Devotion, I intended something less &quot;brutal&quot; than Dominate, but more lasting than Majesty, but once again, without the rulebook, it's kind of hard to create that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T11:04:30-08:00","id":812731,"title":"","content":"Nice catch Rani. I missed that stuff. I didnt want to be harsh about the gift, but I thought it sounded like a bad thing too. Gifts should be good. Banes should be bad. I highly recommend that you get your hands on a 2E book before trying to write more 2E stuff. ^.^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T09:45:24-08:00","id":824384,"title":"","content":"I've changed the Bloodline Gift and suppressed the Devotion (which I wasn't very fond of, and anyway, I think that a Bloodline doesn't necessarily need some special mechanics to be compelling). If also added a paragraph in the Background part. What do you think about it ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}